{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do","id":988291,"title":"Werewolves and the Astral: Wat Do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-16T10:00:48-07:00","id":988291,"title":"Werewolves and the Astral: Wat Do?","content":"So, I've searched through all my books (thank you so much, Onyx Path, for all your lovely searchable PDFs), but I haven't been able to find anything.<br /> <br /> Can Werewolves interact with the Astral in any meaningful way? Do they have any means of entering the Astral (bodily or psychically)? Can they affect Astral beings at all?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T10:06:12-07:00","id":988294,"title":"","content":"Weeeeeellllll, depending on exactly where dreams sit in the whole array of stuff (and I honestly can't remember off the top of my head), Cahalith have the means to prowl around them via the Dream Hunter Facet. Other than that, they have several means of affecting astral entities that have entered the real world by some means and are hanging around in Twilight, and have their usual array of obvious means of interacting with an astral entity that has somehow managed to manifest and become solid.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm not aware of any standard means for werewolves to enter the Astral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T10:35:25-07:00","id":988302,"title":"","content":"At least in first edition, sometimes werewolves dreamt into the Anima Mundi by default. They didn't suffer any deleterious effects from the place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T10:38:27-07:00","id":988303,"title":"","content":"The Astral Realms Book has them naturally wander around the Anima Mundi sometimes when they sleep. They can't get into the Temenos though, because they aren't human. It's unclear whether they have an Oneiros or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T11:12:31-07:00","id":988308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=988303#post988303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Astral Realms Book has them naturally wander around the Anima Mundi sometimes when they sleep. They can't get into the Temenos though, because they aren't human. It's unclear whether they have an Oneiros or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder, though, if they could manage to get into the Primodial Dream, since it seems to be kind of on the border of the Temenos and Anima Mundi, what with it being part of human psychology, but also being connected to the whole &quot;lizard-brain primal fear&quot; part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T04:22:25-07:00","id":989287,"title":"","content":"Not under their own power. Uratha don't have human souls, so don't have an Oneirios and have no cosmological business being in the Temenos, of which the Primordial Dream is part. They do dream, though, and powers that let you enter dreams work on them.<br /> <br /> When Cahalith have one of their prophetic dreams, the Uratha appears in the Anima Mundi's Dreaming Earth, so wherever the Uratha branch away from humans spiritually it's before that.<br /> <br /> Note that Beasts can drag *anyone* into the Temenos by imposing their Lair, inhuman or not.<br /> <br /> Only beings using Integrity, Wisdom, or Satiety have a Temenos. Only those with Integrity or Wisdom have an Oneiros. Almost everything dreams, and only truly aberrant beings like the Strix wouldn't have an Anima Mundi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T05:06:02-07:00","id":989296,"title":"","content":"And Changelings have their Dream Bastions, lacking an Oneiros due to shredded and altered souls. But where do creatures with Humanity fit into it? Are the souls of vampires sufficiently different (or lacking) that they don't have an Oneiros anymore? And by that token, neither would have a Temenos, as Integrity is not Clarity or Humanity.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters... strike me as still having an Oneiros and being part of the Temenos though. Does that mean they have Integrity now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 10-18-2016, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T05:27:03-07:00","id":989299,"title":"","content":"Dream Bastions are in the Hedge. The relationship between the Hedge and the Astral is murky at best and nonexistent at worst - the surest you can be is that dreams are visible from both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T05:34:08-07:00","id":989302,"title":"","content":"Although my personal headcanon is that the &quot;Astral Barrier&quot; mages spend mana to push through between dreams and the Oneiros is actually the Hedge, in a parallel to the way the Gauntlet is not actually a solid wall but does have things living inside it almost no one notices.<br /> <br /> Who knows, if a crossover ever comes up in a book and no one's had a better idea, it might make it into print.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T05:50:20-07:00","id":989304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=989299#post989299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dream Bastions are in the Hedge. The relationship between the Hedge and the Astral is murky at best and nonexistent at worst - the surest you can be is that dreams are visible from both.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dream Bastion remark was tangential to my point, but still a feature of interest since I don't know any other close to human or former mortal being in the CofD that physically disappears into its own dreams. The Hedge-Astral Barrier correlation is a curious thought.<br /> <br /> Still wondering about the fine print implicit in the exclusion of Humanity and the like from your explanation!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T06:02:08-07:00","id":989306,"title":"","content":"Yeah: vampires, changelings, sin-eaters, prometheans, etc don't have Oneiros or Temenos. And Beasts only do because they have a Lair in the Temenos instead of both.<br /> <br /> The only supernatural beings weird enough to not have Integrity but human enough to have a human spiritual landscape are mages. And even then there's differences - the Oneiros of a mage is far more dangerous than normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T06:05:30-07:00","id":989309,"title":"","content":"Very interesting. Thanks for the answer Dave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T06:12:10-07:00","id":989311,"title":"","content":"So, being in a Wolf-Blooded's Oneiros during their First Change is probably an interesting experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T06:20:51-07:00","id":989315,"title":"","content":"And potentially a fatal one!<br /> <br /> Although now I wonder what it looks like if you're in someone's soul when they get embraced. Or, for that matter, die.<br /> <br /> The answer is almost certainly &quot;you get dumped into Temenos&quot; but still. Story hook!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T06:41:01-07:00","id":989322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=989315#post989315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And potentially a fatal one!<br /> <br /> Although now I wonder what it looks like if you're in someone's soul when they get embraced. Or, for that matter, die.<br /> <br /> The answer is almost certainly &quot;you get dumped into Temenos&quot; but still. Story hook!</div> </div> </div> </div>Or what if you get dragged to whatever Vampires have instead of Oneiros, and have to try and 1) Figure out what the hell just happened, 2) Figure out how to get free, and 3) Try not to get devoured by the newly-embraced Vampire's Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T08:29:37-07:00","id":989358,"title":"","content":"Now I'm also curious what happens if you fall asleep while a guest in a Beast's Lair. What happens then? Where do you go? Do you appear in Dream Form in the Lair and witness your own sleeping body? If you're a Changeling, do you end up going to the Hedge anyway, or does a Dream Bastion just form right there in the Lair?<br /> <br /> Inquiring minds wish to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:00:12-07:00","id":989374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=989306#post989306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah: vampires, changelings, sin-eaters, prometheans, etc don't have Oneiros or Temenos. And Beasts only do because they have a Lair in the Temenos instead of both.<br /> <br /> The only supernatural beings weird enough to not have Integrity but human enough to have a human spiritual landscape are mages. And even then there's differences - the Oneiros of a mage is far more dangerous than normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>But wait don't Sin-Eaters still have a human soul? It just has a Ghost clinging on to it. So shouldn't they still have an Oneiros?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T10:33:17-07:00","id":989427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=989374#post989374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But wait don't Sin-Eaters still have a human soul? It just has a Ghost clinging on to it. So shouldn't they still have an Oneiros?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe that ghost's presence interferes with the soul, so the Underworld stands in to replace their Temenos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T10:40:39-07:00","id":989429,"title":"","content":"A geist seems to be doing a lot more than just clinging onto a sin-eater's soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:29:25-07:00","id":989459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=989302#post989302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although my personal headcanon is that the &quot;Astral Barrier&quot; mages spend mana to push through between dreams and the Oneiros is actually the Hedge, in a parallel to the way the Gauntlet is not actually a solid wall but does have things living inside it almost no one notices.<br /> <br /> <br /> Who knows, if a crossover ever comes up in a book and no one's had a better idea, it might make it into print.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Will you be one of the authors on the upcoming Crossover Chronicles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:03:07-07:00","id":989591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=989287#post989287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Only beings using Integrity, Wisdom, or Satiety have a Temenos. Only those with Integrity or Wisdom have an Oneiros. Almost everything dreams, and only truly aberrant beings like the Strix wouldn't have an Anima Mundi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do Ghosts stand in this? Do they 'dream', as well? Given that they have no soul, they don't have an Oneiros and a Temenos, right? Perhaps only an Anima Mundi...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:24:50-07:00","id":989607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=989591#post989591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where do Ghosts stand in this? Do they 'dream', as well? Given that they have no soul, they don't have an Oneiros and a Temenos, right? Perhaps only an Anima Mundi...</div> </div> </div> </div>If they do dream, and they get sent to the Anima Mundi, that might serve to explain why they lose their identities as they age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T11:30:58-07:00","id":989979,"title":"","content":"What level do you guys think a Rite that would let a Werewolf enter a trance to enter the Anima Mundi would be? It seems like it should be possible even if it was rare and difficult to attain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T11:37:40-07:00","id":989983,"title":"","content":"Probably four dots. First edition had a rite that opened Avernian gates at four dots, and Open Moon Gates, too. So it sounds like opening temporary portals is four dots.<br /> <br /> Question is, what for? Obviously there's a Firstborn hiding out there. But it doesn't seem like a place werewolves would have much to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-19-2016, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:04:22-07:00","id":990056,"title":"","content":"In the Astral Realms book there are Naturae entities in the Dreaming Earth that can grant Influence dots in the physical world over their purview, from racoon lords to the embodiment of Toronto's ecosystem. That's useful for anyone. And I could imagine giving some kind of reward to Uratha who thoroughly explore the Dreaming Earth reflection of their territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:14:56-07:00","id":990063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=989979#post989979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What level do you guys think a Rite that would let a Werewolf enter a trance to enter the Anima Mundi would be? It seems like it should be possible even if it was rare and difficult to attain.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt's unlikely that such a rite would be possible; opening gateways to such distant realms is mostly beyond the reach of the Shadow's laws and cycles. I can think of some metaphysical justifications for such a rite but they're pretty esoteric.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor much the same reason, I don't think I'd create a rite that can open an Avernian gate either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T14:47:19-07:00","id":990110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=990063#post990063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIt's unlikely that such a rite would be possible; opening gateways to such distant realms is mostly beyond the reach of the Shadow's laws and cycles. I can think of some metaphysical justifications for such a rite but they're pretty esoteric.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's what makes it such a good plot point, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bFor much the same reason, I don't think I'd create a rite that can open an Avernian gate either. </div> </div> </div>Well, I would assume that, if not a Rite, a Death-related spirit or Fetish of sufficient power reasonably could open an Avernian gate, though.<br /> <br /> Or they could suck up to a Sin-Eater or Mage, I suppose, but that's too easy an answer, and relies on a Storyteller and group being willing to spill Mage or Sin-Eater on their Werewolf game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:04:17-07:00","id":990125,"title":"","content":"Considering how Death and Dreams are pretty major concepts that have a place in the Shadow I think it would be a solid route to have lvl 4 Rites that turn Loci attuned to them into outright gateways. Now, surviving the trip over there is your own thing. And I'm pretty sure Death Wolf might laugh at you for fucking it up.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:08:22-07:00","id":990126,"title":"","content":"I think Avernian gates, and Hedge gates, sometimes have 'mundane' ways to open, like a blood sacrifice or something.<br /> <br /> Still, it's easier to find Influences in the hisil, where werewolves likely have more power. Get Lodge Sorcery, or a fetish.<br /> <br /> I think Death Wolf would be impressed, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T05:56:54-07:00","id":990378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=990063#post990063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIt's unlikely that such a rite would be possible; opening gateways to such distant realms is mostly beyond the reach of the Shadow's laws and cycles. I can think of some metaphysical justifications for such a rite but they're pretty esoteric.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor much the same reason, I don't think I'd create a rite that can open an Avernian gate either.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wasn't thinking of a gateway, I was thinking that the Rite would allow the participants to dream their way in like Cahaliths do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:22:30-07:00","id":991982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=989315#post989315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And potentially a fatal one!<br /> <br /> Although now I wonder what it looks like if you're in someone's soul when they get embraced. Or, for that matter, die.<br /> <br /> The answer is almost certainly &quot;you get dumped into Temenos&quot; but still. Story hook!</div> </div> </div> </div>If they don't have an Oneiros, does that mean they don't have a Daimon, and so therefore never second-guess their actions? Don't Goetia in your Oneiros represent critical concepts important to your self-conception and personality?<br /> <br /> How do Werewolves interact with collective unconsciousness (as expressed through the Temenos) if they no longer have any connection to them? Which, I admit, is a subtle thing with no mechanical reflection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 10-23-2016, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:39:20-07:00","id":991991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=989287#post989287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not under their own power. Uratha don't have human souls, so don't have an Oneirios and have no cosmological business being in the Temenos, of which the Primordial Dream is part. They do dream, though, and powers that let you enter dreams work on them.<br /> <br /> When Cahalith have one of their prophetic dreams, the Uratha appears in the Anima Mundi's Dreaming Earth, so wherever the Uratha branch away from humans spiritually it's before that.<br /> <br /> Note that Beasts can drag *anyone* into the Temenos by imposing their Lair, inhuman or not.<br /> <br /> Only beings using Integrity, Wisdom, or Satiety have a Temenos. Only those with Integrity or Wisdom have an Oneiros. Almost everything dreams, and only truly aberrant beings like the Strix wouldn't have an Anima Mundi.</div> </div> </div> </div>This pretty much flies in the face of Rites of Spring as far as I'm concerned. No one 'has' a Temenos, that's contrary to the entire notion of what 'The' Temenos is. Beasts do not have 'a' Temenos, they have a Lair that exists within 'The' Temenos, and can theoretically be accessed by anyone wandering it if they can find it.<br /> <br /> If, in your Head-Canon, the Oneiros is the Hedge, how then do Changelings work Oneiromancy on vampires and werewolves if they have no Oneiros? It's not terribly consistent. Claiming that werewolves have no Oneiros denies that they are wolf 'and' man. It denies the duality of the concept. The human bit of them is what help makes the game a horror game as they deal with their own actions and the instincts that come from their spirit half.<br /> <br /> Likewise with vampire, I'd be much more willing to accept that as a Vampire's humanity drops, their Oneiros breaks down in some massive way. Vampires very obviously have souls, this is established. Because they have souls, they have an Oneiros. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:47:47-07:00","id":991994,"title":"","content":"Werewolves aren't wolf and man, they're werewolves, neither wolf or man. Their duality is between the spirit and the flesh, not human or wolf.<br /> <br /> But obviously your head-canon would require you to appreciate that Oneiromancy is just a term associated with the interpretation of dreams as it is in real life, and not the specific Oneiros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:16:00-07:00","id":992005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=991994#post991994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves aren't wolf and man, they're werewolves, neither wolf or man. Their duality is between the spirit and the flesh, not human or wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf the Forsaken 2nd Edition 'Themes'</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf is built on the idea of having one foot on either side of a boundary. Characters aren\u2019t neutral \u2014 if one side is black and the other is white, most werewolves try to be just as black as they are white. Some make the mistake of thinking that means \u201cgray,\u201d while others ignore the boundary in favor of one side or another. Being a werewolf means stepping up and taking responsibility without going too far.<br /> <br /> Focus too much on the <b>human </b>and you will be trapped in your unchanging flesh, unable to understand what you really are. Focus too much on the monster and you will fade from the world and never see your loved ones again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. The very definition of the word Werewolf is Man Wolf. The dichotomy of wolf and human, spirit and flesh, is the defining <b>theme</b> of Werewolf the Forsaken. They are very much still human, this diminishes somewhat as their Primal Urge increases, and if their Harmony shifts too far toward spirit. Conversely, a werewolf who is 'too human' will become trapped in their own flesh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=991994#post991994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But obviously your head-canon would require you to appreciate that Oneiromancy is just a term associated with the interpretation of dreams as it is in real life, and not the specific Oneiros.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oneiromancy is not the interpretation of dreams, it entails actively taking a hand in them and at times entering them. To perform Oneiromancy in Changeling, one must often be in the Hedge. According to Dave, the Hedge and the Oneiros are the same thing - which would explain why Oneiromancy is performed in the Hedge and how it affects the Oneiros of mortals. What it doesn't explain is why a Changeling can perform Oneiromancy on Werewolves and Vampires from the Hedge if they don't have an Oneiros.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:18:45-07:00","id":992007,"title":"","content":"Even the naming of things like Pack Tactics in The Pack follows a Man/Wolf interpretation there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:41:53-07:00","id":992022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=991991#post991991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This pretty much flies in the face of Rites of Spring as far as I'm concerned. No one 'has' a Temenos, that's contrary to the entire notion of what 'The' Temenos is. Beasts do not have 'a' Temenos, they have a Lair that exists within 'The' Temenos, and can theoretically be accessed by anyone wandering it if they can find it.<br /> <br /> If, in your Head-Canon, the Oneiros is the Hedge, how then do Changelings work Oneiromancy on vampires and werewolves if they have no Oneiros? It's not terribly consistent. Claiming that werewolves have no Oneiros denies that they are wolf 'and' man. It denies the duality of the concept. The human bit of them is what help makes the game a horror game as they deal with their own actions and the instincts that come from their spirit half.<br /> <br /> Likewise with vampire, I'd be much more willing to accept that as a Vampire's humanity drops, their Oneiros breaks down in some massive way. Vampires very obviously have souls, this is established. Because they have souls, they have an Oneiros.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Lemme explain, because I think you may have misunderstood what Dave meant. Vampires etc. don't <i>access</i> to the Temenos, I think is what he intended to say.<br /> <br /> And I don't think Dave meant that the Oneiros is the Hedge, but more like it's an &quot;Astral Gauntlet.&quot; In most contexts, it acts like a barrier between the physical and the Astral, but it's also its own distinct realm that has its own inhabitants that most Astrally-inclined beings never see, like the Gauntlet between the physical and the Shadow. Under this interpretation, Changelings perform Oneiromancy on things like Werewolves not by entering the Oneiros, but instead following their Astral path, to wherever they go. So they touch a human's Oneiros, but with Beasts they touch the Lair, and with Vampires, they touch whatever Vampires have instead of an Oneiros (which is probably where the Beast lives).<br /> <br /> I could be interpreting it wrong, though.<br /> <br /> Though, I would not want to be inside a Vampire's pseudo-Oneiros. Especially not at low humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:46:50-07:00","id":992027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992022#post992022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lemme explain, because I think you may have misunderstood what Dave meant. Vampires etc. don't <i>access</i> to the Temenos, I think is what he intended to say.<br /> <br /> And I don't think Dave meant that the Oneiros is the Hedge, but more like it's an &quot;Astral Gauntlet.&quot; In most contexts, it acts like a barrier between the physical and the Astral, but it's also its own distinct realm that has its own inhabitants that most Astrally-inclined beings never see, like the Gauntlet between the physical and the Shadow. Under this interpretation, Changelings perform Oneiromancy on things like Werewolves not by entering the Oneiros, but instead following their Astral path, to wherever they go. So they touch a human's Oneiros, but with Beasts they touch the Lair, and with Vampires, they touch whatever Vampires have instead of an Oneiros (which is probably where the Beast lives).<br /> <br /> I could be interpreting it wrong, though.<br /> <br /> Though, I would not want to be inside a Vampire's pseudo-Oneiros. Especially not at low humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only specific types of dreams, including the Cahalith auspice ability, takes a werewolf into the Anima Mundi. However. There is no reason to believe that they otherwise have no Oneiros, or that they don't deal with their own soul while dreaming the way everyone else does. It's still contrary to Rites of Spring, Mind magic in earlier supplements, and so on, to believe otherwise.<br /> <br /> I don't believe a Changeling could work Oneiromancy on Beasts, because Beasts don't dream, they reverse possess their Horrors in their sleep. They do not have a soul after The Devouring, and therefor they would not have an Oneiros, their new soul is reflected in their Horror and their Lair, and that serves all the purposes an Oneiros does for everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":".  Spelling and grammar corrections, and wanted to clarify the Beast issue. 10-23-2016, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:07:13-07:00","id":992042,"title":"","content":"Valid points, there are definitely conflicts. but,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992027#post992027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe a Changeling could work Oneiromancy on Beasts, because Beasts don't dream, they reverse possess their Horrors in their sleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if there's really much of a distinction between the two here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:27:21-07:00","id":992058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992005#post992005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Emphasis mine. The very definition of the word Werewolf is Man Wolf. The dichotomy of wolf and human, spirit and flesh, is the defining <b>theme</b> of Werewolf the Forsaken. They are very much still human, this diminishes somewhat as their Primal Urge increases, and if their Harmony shifts too far toward spirit. Conversely, a werewolf who is 'too human' will become trapped in their own flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves aren't human at all. Their flesh side is inclined towards human behavior but isn't limited by human needs. It says this on the next page, 'We were born and raised looking like humans, but that is a disguise.' Werewolves not being human is a point repeatedly made throughout the book.<br /> <br /> And if you get past the loose introduction of themes and read further into it, you'll see that it is not just a matter of human and beast. 'One one hand, she's a hunter wearing the skin of human and wolf, a creature of nature unlike anything else in the natural world. She's flesh incarnate. On the other hand, she's a creature of spirit, an entity that exists among the denizens of the Hisil, feeding on the ephemeral Essence of the world of Spirit. These two extremes pull the Forsaken in two directions.' Wolf and human are both firmly on the flesh side of the flesh versus spirit equation.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5226_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5226\" data-vbnamecard=\"5226\">Jachra</a> And that's a different thing than their Harmony, instead focusing on how they choose to go about the hunt.<br /> <br /> Regarding Oneiromancy, I was pointing out that the literal definition of the word refers to the interpretation of dreams, not specifically dealing with a magical Oneiros belonging to certain people in the Chronicles of Darkness. As Dave has said, most everyone dreams, and a Changeling would be able to reach their dreams because they don't deal with the magical Oneiros itself, they deal with dreams.<br /> <br /> And anyways, Dave didn't say the Oneiros is the Hedge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although my personal headcanon is that the &quot;Astral Barrier&quot; mages spend mana to push through between dreams and the Oneiros is actually the Hedge, in a parallel to the way the Gauntlet is not actually a solid wall but does have things living inside it almost no one notices. </div> </div> </div>He said the barrier between dreams and the Oneiros is the Hedge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:33:34-07:00","id":992064,"title":"","content":"Solana, while your argument is very interesting, I never said the Hedge is the Oneiros, I said it might be the Astral Barrier...<br /> <br /> (sees Nofather's post)<br /> <br /> Yeah. That.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:32:19-07:00","id":992100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992007#post992007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the naming of things like Pack Tactics in The Pack follows a Man/Wolf interpretation there.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't mean that werewolves are human or wolf. nofather had it right - they're werewolves. Their own thing. The man/wolf thing comes because they spend their formative years in human societies, then get near overloaded with primal wolffish hunting instincts when they change. Finding the balance between spirit and flesh gives them Harmony, finding the werewolf balance between reason and instinct helps their hunt.<br /> <br /> Naming Pack Tactics along wolf/man lines are because that's evocative language. I could have called them instinct and reason (and briefly did) but that's more clinical, and didn't feel primal enough for what I was going for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:49:20-07:00","id":992105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992100#post992100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This doesn't mean that werewolves are human or wolf. nofather had it right - they're werewolves. Their own thing. The man/wolf thing comes because they spend their formative years in human societies, then get near overloaded with primal wolffish hunting instincts when they change. Finding the balance between spirit and flesh gives them Harmony, finding the werewolf balance between reason and instinct helps their hunt.<br /> <br /> Naming Pack Tactics along wolf/man lines are because that's evocative language. I could have called them instinct and reason (and briefly did) but that's more clinical, and didn't feel primal enough for what I was going for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's good to know, because Nofather's point came specifically from a first person perspective statement, and it's been my experience that first person narrators in these books are usually trying to compensate for something. Something akin to vampires being dismissive over how important Humanity is, etc. A werewolf can assert that &quot;I'm not human, was never human.&quot; But the reality is that they were wolf-blooded before they changed, not werewolves waiting to happen. If that weren't the case, then there would be ways to know if someone is going to change or not, and it would make more sense for auspice to be determined at birth, the way it is in Apocalypse. <br /> <br /> Because of this, and because a werewolf's 'soul' is removed exactly the same way a human's is, I believed the themes to swing more toward Human/Wolf-Spirit rather than just Spirit and a generalized 'flesh'. There are other things like - mating with humans is a Harmony breaking point at 3 or Lower, but mating with wolves apparently isn't, so Spirit and Wolf become conflated in my mind. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992064#post992064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solana, while your argument is very interesting, I never said the Hedge is the Oneiros, I said it might be the Astral Barrier...<br /> <br /> (sees Nofather's post)<br /> <br /> Yeah. That.</div> </div> </div> </div>My mistake, I misread the part where you said 'Astral Barrier'. The notion that the Hedge is equivalent to the Gauntlet in the Astral Realms doesn't really sit with my head-canon because my head-canon divides the soul into five parts, one for each of the subtle Arcana. Stating that the edge, an emanation of Fate, overlaps in some way with the Astral would diminish the importance Fate has in the composition of the soul, to my eyes. Likewise with the Underworld and Death, the Hisil and Spirit, and the Astral Realms with Mind. That said, I did have to create a whole different realm (the Realms Apocryphal) in order to fit Prime into that system, so it's entirely head-canon for me as well. <br /> <br /> I maintain that Vampires and Werewolves have souls and conscious identities, therefor they must have Oneiroi, however. I don't think a Changeling would be 'human enough' to get back if they were so far gone as to no longer have an Oneiros. If a werewolf is really so much Spirit that they don't have an Oneiros, then certain other things should be true as well, like manipulating them with Spirit instead of Mind. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:57:39-07:00","id":992110,"title":"","content":"A werewolf &quot;oneiros&quot; is something so alien that neither beasts nor mages can access it, but it still counts as a mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:41:27-07:00","id":992155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992105#post992105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My mistake, I misread the part where you said 'Astral Barrier'. The notion that the Hedge is equivalent to the Gauntlet in the Astral Realms doesn't really sit with my head-canon because my head-canon divides the soul into five parts, one for each of the subtle Arcana. Stating that the edge, an emanation of Fate, overlaps in some way with the Astral would diminish the importance Fate has in the composition of the soul, to my eyes. Likewise with the Underworld and Death, the Hisil and Spirit, and the Astral Realms with Mind. That said, I did have to create a whole different realm (the Realms Apocryphal) in order to fit Prime into that system, so it's entirely head-canon for me as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kinda neat I'd be interested to hear more about it. Though, couldn't you assign the Supernal World itself to Prime? Considering Prime is all about the manipulation of truths and supernal symbols?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T19:06:28-07:00","id":992172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992155#post992155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's kinda neat I'd be interested to hear more about it. Though, couldn't you assign the Supernal World itself to Prime? Considering Prime is all about the manipulation of truths and supernal symbols?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The issue is that The Aether is the Supernal Prime realm. Supernal Arcadia is the Supernal Fate realm, Stygia is the Supernal Death Realm, Pandemonium is the Supernal Mind/Astral Realms, and the Primal Wilds are the Supernal Hisil/Spirit realm. In my version of the cosmology, these supernal concepts are reflected imperfectly in the fallen world thanks to the shenannigans of the Exarchs. The Hedge and fallen Arcadia are a fallen reflection of Supernal Arcadia, and so on. The Aether is a realm of Prime, perfect objective Truth with a capital T. Realms Apocryphal are a fallen version of that where everything is true and everything isn't, it's all purely subjective. The spirits that inhabit it are often angelic, and when they possess mortals, those mortals either acquire Obsessions outright, or else act as though they do.<br /> <br /> There was also a lot tying it into Hallows and certain types of Leylines, but it's been awhile since we ran that game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T06:21:12-07:00","id":992349,"title":"","content":"Oh, okay. We're talking about your personal version of the cosmology.<br /> <br /> That's cool, then. Say werewolves are included in the temenos in your games all you like. Sounds cool.<br /> <br /> In Mage, and Beast, the two games about the Astral, they're not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T07:45:32-07:00","id":992380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992105#post992105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a werewolf is really so much Spirit that they don't have an Oneiros, then certain other things should be true as well, like manipulating them with Spirit instead of Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Mage book does have the following as an example of how Mage Sight might interpret a werewolf:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#004E6D\"><span style=\"font-family:FuturaT-Book\">\u201cYou can see with Spirit Sight that she appears to be composed as much of spirit as flesh \u2014 she isn\u2019t possessed, since the spirit isn\u2019t simply riding her. It looks more like her body \u2014 her whole Pattern \u2014 is in constant flux between ephemera and material.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> Taking this as face value (which, admittedly, might not be the intention since it's just in a side bar) using Spirit should be just as viable as Mind and Life. But I haven't read WtF yet so I can't speak about that perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T08:08:45-07:00","id":992388,"title":"","content":"Werewolves tend to get the benefits of being a spirit whilst dodging the downsides. <br /> <br /> Like, a spirit two ranks or more higher than another counts as it's bane and can deal aggravated damage to it. Werewolves can deal damage like that if their honorary rank is high enough, but don't have to worry about it themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T08:19:02-07:00","id":992390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992380#post992380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the Mage book does have the following as an example of how Mage Sight might interpret a werewolf:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#004E6D\"><span style=\"font-family:FuturaT-Book\">\u201cYou can see with Spirit Sight that she appears to be composed as much of spirit as flesh \u2014 she isn\u2019t possessed, since the spirit isn\u2019t simply riding her. It looks more like her body \u2014 her whole Pattern \u2014 is in constant flux between ephemera and material.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> Taking this as face value (which, admittedly, might not be the intention since it's just in a side bar) using Spirit should be just as viable as Mind and Life. But I haven't read WtF yet so I can't speak about that perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it depends what you wanna do. They still have a (relatively) human mind, so their consciousnesses are probably still governed by Mind, and their physical bodies are still affected by Life since they're still physical and fleshy (kinda like Pangaeans, huh), but they still have a lot of spiritual components (Gifts and Renown, for example) that would definitely fall under Spirit.<br /> <br /> ...Come to think of it, maybe Werewolves are just the last remaining race of Pangaeans? Managing to keep themselves neither spirit nor flesh by careful balance and Luna's blessing? I mean, it would explain a lot, and considering Father Wolf was Pangaean, it'd make some sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T08:45:17-07:00","id":992397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992390#post992390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Come to think of it, maybe Werewolves are just the last remaining race of Pangaeans? Managing to keep themselves neither spirit nor flesh by careful balance and Luna's blessing? I mean, it would explain a lot, and considering Father Wolf was Pangaean, it'd make some sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's why they're Forsaken. One of the reasons, at least. Their homeland is gone.<br /> <br /> They're torn between the spirit and the flesh because there is no Pangaea anymore, no place where both meet. And to make ends meet, to fulfill their Sacred Hunt, they have to use spirit rituals instead of just hunting in Pangaea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T09:44:16-07:00","id":992423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992349#post992349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, okay. We're talking about your personal version of the cosmology.<br /> <br /> That's cool, then. Say werewolves are included in the temenos in your games all you like. Sounds cool.<br /> <br /> In Mage, and Beast, the two games about the Astral, they're not.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do spirits dream? There's a couple of mention of such in a few sources in the first edition, with according fetishes that allow to view, and interact with such dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:11:19-07:00","id":992444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992423#post992423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do spirits dream? There's a couple of mention of such in a few sources in the first edition, with according fetishes that allow to view, and interact with such dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Uratha do dream, they just don't have a personal Oneiros, they end up in the Anima Mundi. Presumably something similiar happens to Spirits (It may make a kind of sense in that the Anima Mundi is about exploring the soul of the world, and that's what Spirits are in a certain sense, or at least they're often referred to as such in Awakening).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:31:59-07:00","id":992455,"title":"","content":"I think something most people miss is that the Oneiros is not the first plane of the Astral Realms (well, it is the first of the &quot;Astral proper&quot;). People (which I believe includes humans, werewolves, vampires and possibly even spirits, though don't quote me on that) simply dream in their personal dream plane. A common mortal does not enter their own soul (Oneiros) just because they fall asleep and start dreaming. They're simply just in their personal dream plane. Werewolves (and spirits) sometimes end up in Anima Mundi, but they should also usually just have common dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:41:58-07:00","id":992467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992444#post992444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Uratha do dream, they just don't have a personal Oneiros, they end up in the Anima Mundi. Presumably something similiar happens to Spirits (It may make a kind of sense in that the Anima Mundi is about exploring the soul of the world, and that's what Spirits are in a certain sense, or at least they're often referred to as such in Awakening).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So does a Changeling or a Mage or a Vampire invading the dreams of a werewolf risk exposure to the ecstatic winds, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:48:09-07:00","id":992472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992467#post992467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does a Changeling or a Mage or a Vampire invading the dreams of a werewolf risk exposure to the ecstatic winds, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because Dreams are on other layer of Astral.<br /> <br /> From the outside, Astral looks like this:<br /> 0. Dreams - every dreaming being have those. They like one or two scene of Oneiros <b>without </b>need of having Oneiros. Changelings go here.<br /> 1. Oneiros - realm of personal soul. All memories, hopes and fears are here - if you got one, you are human enought to be... well, human.<br /> 2. Temeons - realm of humanity. Shared ideas in human kind.<br /> 3. Anima Mundi - realm of world-soul. Shared concepts across entire universe.<br /> WAS: 4. Supernal Realms - realm of how world <b>could</b> be.<br /> <br /> Where mages can go from 0 to 3, werewolves just go in to 0 or sometimes 3 and changelings are all operating on 0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:48:13-07:00","id":992473,"title":"","content":"I was wrong about werewolves dreaming in their personal dream planes.<br /> From Astral Realms, p.80:<br /> <span style=\"color:#636366\"><span style=\"font-family:DeadHistoryRoman\">&quot;</span></span><span style=\"color:#636366\"><span style=\"font-family:DeadHistoryRoman\">The Uratha o<span style=\"font-family:DeadHistoryBold\"><span style=\"font-family:DeadHistoryRoman\">ften roam the Dreaming Earth. To them, doing so is no stranger than a human exploring his own dreamscape. In fact, the practice is so unexceptional that werewolves don\u2019t think of their travels as much more than a holy dream.&quot;</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992467#post992467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does a Changeling or a Mage or a Vampire invading the dreams of a werewolf risk exposure to the ecstatic winds, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the same side bar:<br /> <span style=\"color:#636366\"><span style=\"font-family:DeadHistoryRoman\"><span style=\"font-family:DeadHistoryBold\"><span style=\"font-family:DeadHistoryRoman\">&quot;Werewolves don\u2019t feel the Ecstatic Wind because they\u2019re capable of thinking and acting similar to the other inhabitants of the realm.&quot;</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> If the invader ends up in Anima Mundi, yes. They're not acclimatized to the realm the same way as a werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:10:05-07:00","id":992484,"title":"","content":"Ohhhh, I see.<br /> <br /> Yeah. A human's dreams are not their Oneiros. You can watch someone's dreams from inside their Oneiros, the same as you can watch them from the Hedge, but the two are not the same. <br /> <br /> Just because something isn't human enough to have an Oneiros and/or participate in creating the Temenos, doesn't mean they don't dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:59:15-07:00","id":992519,"title":"","content":"Thank you for clearing that up for me. From a storytelling perspective I'm still not sure what the advantage of removing Oneiroi from different supernatural beings might be, but that's the purposes of head-canon I suppose.<br /> <br /> I'd like to thank everyone again for being patient with me and answering my questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T12:28:06-07:00","id":992529,"title":"","content":"If the Oneiros is the soul, then I totally get why most supernaturals don't have an Oneiros. What I don't get is why there's no mention of what they could have instead. A vampire's Oneiros could be its Beast and its Humanity at odds with each other, which would be extremely interesting (and dangerous) to explore. Instead of a Daimon trying to better its dreamer the vampire has its Beast thrashing against chains imposed on it by the vampire's Humanity. The weaker the Humanity, the more freedom the Beast has to stalk and hunt any intruders. But I'm leaving it at that since the thread is about werewolves in the Astral; not vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T12:34:31-07:00","id":992533,"title":"","content":"Presumably it's because the only ones who've been able to study the Oneiros are mages. Werewolves, vampires and so forth don't have any Awakened.<br /> <br /> But it could just be a number thing. Humanity vastly outnumbers the other gameline supernaturals. Or an understanding thing, as they haven't had the great studies in philosophy and soul-searching humanity has had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-24-2016, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T13:36:42-07:00","id":992548,"title":"","content":"Werewolves are probably in a similar boat to vampires. They don't have an oneiros because they have something that fulfils the same function that in no way resembles an oneiros whatsoever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:42:40-07:00","id":993175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992529#post992529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Oneiros is the soul, then I totally get why most supernaturals don't have an Oneiros. What I don't get is why there's no mention of what they could have instead. A vampire's Oneiros could be its Beast and its Humanity at odds with each other, which would be extremely interesting (and dangerous) to explore. Instead of a Daimon trying to better its dreamer the vampire has its Beast thrashing against chains imposed on it by the vampire's Humanity. The weaker the Humanity, the more freedom the Beast has to stalk and hunt any intruders. But I'm leaving it at that since the thread is about werewolves in the Astral; not vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Doylist Answer: Wordcount, Mage doesn't really have the space in its corebook to dive into that much detail about other gamelines.<br /> <br /> Watsonion Answer: It's a Mystery. Sound like an interesting Obsession to play out for a Mastigos and his friends ( a Thyrsus for werewolves, a Moros for Sin-eaters, etc.)<br /> <br /> Would be an interesting thread to start in the Mage forums maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T19:48:46-07:00","id":993847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=990063#post990063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIt's unlikely that such a rite would be possible; opening gateways to such distant realms is mostly beyond the reach of the Shadow's laws and cycles. I can think of some metaphysical justifications for such a rite but they're pretty esoteric.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor much the same reason, I don't think I'd create a rite that can open an Avernian gate either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Coming a little late to the party, but asking anyway:<br /> <br /> Aren't the Aeon of Spirit and the Aeon of Life the only ones that can leave the farthest shores of the Astral Realms? If Uratha are Life+Spirit, couldn't them find those Aeons and devise a rite to access the Anima Mundi?<br /> <br /> Also, Werewolves are Pangaeans, and Pangaeans had access to Arcana. I don't think it is a very far stretch to say that they would have come from the same place as mages, the Times Before. This might be metaphysically enough to justify some rare rites to access the Anima Mundi, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T20:15:01-07:00","id":993856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=993847#post993847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't the Aeon of Spirit and the Aeon of Life the only ones that can leave the farthest shores of the Astral Realms?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Copse of the Primal Wild is rumored to be the remaining axis mundi, but no, the Aeon of Fate has been a slippery bastard in at least two of his incarnations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Uratha are Life+Spirit, couldn't them find those Aeons and devise a rite to access the Anima Mundi? </div> </div> </div>They don't <i>need</i> a rite to access the Anima Mundi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Werewolves are Pangaeans </div> </div> </div>Neither the Uratha nor the Firstborn are Pangaeans. Pending some story-specific discovery, every Pangaean that existed is dead, gone, or nigh-irreversibly changed into something else in the modern day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T22:41:42-07:00","id":993901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992423#post992423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do spirits dream? There's a couple of mention of such in a few sources in the first edition, with according fetishes that allow to view, and interact with such dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>They lie down in their bed and sleep until they wildly halliucinate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:51:39-07:00","id":994723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=992349#post992349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, okay. We're talking about your personal version of the cosmology.<br /> <br /> That's cool, then. Say werewolves are included in the temenos in your games all you like. Sounds cool.<br /> <br /> In Mage, and Beast, the two games about the Astral, they're not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The degree of deliberate taking my statements out of context is disgusting here, Dave. I don't appreciate that at all.<br /> <br /> I mentioned in off hand fashion something that was 'my' head canon, and someone said 'that's cool' and implied they'd like for me to elaborate. So I did, while quoting them, speaking specifically to them. Don't act like I didn't provide canonical reasons for my assertion that Werewolves, Vampires, and Changelings have an Oneiros, based on their having souls and very clearly a Mind component to their very identities. I tried to step out of this thread on good terms only to have shade thrown at me? I wouldn't have even seen this if a friend hadn't pointed it out.<br /> <br /> I've yet to see any reason from you as to why they shouldn't have an Oneiros, aside from &quot;They just don't, because they're not human enough&quot; with the unspoken caveat that you are a writer, and that's all the justification you need to give.<br /> <br /> Edit: And you're doing the Temenos thing, again, when all of my statements were about the Oneiros, that is to say - the expression of the personal soul within the Astral Realms. The Temenos is still the collective unconscious, and the only time I brought it up was in correcting you after you said 'having a temenos', which is by definition impossible, the Temenos literally belongs to everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-28-2016, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:07:28-07:00","id":994774,"title":"","content":"Werewolves don't have souls. They're part spirit. They've never been depicted having an Oneiros, but do have a connection to the deepest Astral layer somehow.<br /> Changelings have damaged souls from the thorns, when the state of them is mentioned at all. They do not have an Oneiros and are literally incapable of entering the Temenos, as per Dancers in the Dusk.<br /> <br /> Your &quot;Correction&quot; about the Temenos falls flat because of the difference between being an active participant in making it (ie, being human, or a Beast) and being someone who doesn't have that inherent connection but intrudes into it with a power (like Demons can). That's what I was saying about &quot;having a Temenos&quot;; werewolves don't have human enough souls to participate in it, so barring unusual gifts would just skip right past it. Or quite possibly have an entirely different astral realm all their own, before joining up to the humans again in the Anima Mundi.<br /> <br /> The Temenos doesn't belong to everyone. It belongs to humans. The <i>Anima Mundi</i> belongs to everyone.<br /> <br /> Think of it as branching trees<br /> <br /> ( humans ) ( werewolves )<br /> <br /> Oneiros Oneiros Oneiros Oneiros Oneiros Oneiros Oneiros ??? ??? ???<br /> \\................. / .........\\............. /............ \\............. /........... /.......... \\ ....| ..../<br /> .\\................/........... \\ .........../.............. \\ .........../........... /............ \\... |... /<br /> ..-------------------------Temenos ------------------------------------ .......--?????-<br /> ................................\\ .................................................. ..................../<br /> .................................\\................ .................................................. .. /<br /> ....................................-----------Anima Mundi----------------------------<br /> <br /> If Werewolves have an astral within whatever it is they have instead of souls that permeate their entire spirit/flesh hybrid bodies, it might have analogous layers to Oneiros and Temenos, but a realm-of-an-individual-werewolf's spirit would not be an Oneiros, and a realm of all Werewolves would not be the Temenos. As far as we're concerned, the question-mark realms don't exist, and werewolves just go straight from their dreams to the Anima Mundi. But again, if you want to invent strange new worlds to explore, go for it.<br /> <br /> EDIT to fix ascii diagram.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 10-28-2016, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:19:10-07:00","id":994776,"title":"","content":"There are good game-design reasons for keeping the Oneiros and Temenos humans (and Beasts) only, foremost among them the lack of need to explain the Astral in every single game. It's there when games like Beast and Demon want to use it. It's ignorable when games like Changeling and Werewolf don't want to use it, and that's all the justification I need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:44:55-07:00","id":994798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994774#post994774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves don't have souls. They're part spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure? Their book makes repeated mentions to the werewolf's soul, as well as their being part spirit, but still maintaining a soul, from a fluff and mechanical point of view. Forge Empty Wolf, for instance says, 'The idigam may touch a werewolf and, with a Power + Finesse roll contested by the victim's Resolve + Composure + Primal Urge, tear the soul free and replace it with a spirit or soul of the idigam's choice.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:49:36-07:00","id":994803,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but they're idigam. They can rip out a werewolf's &quot;soul&quot; using what is notably a <i>different</i> power to the one that lets them rip out a human's soul. If the two were one and the same then it wouldn't require different abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:57:33-07:00","id":994809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994803#post994803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but they're idigam. They can rip out a werewolf's &quot;soul&quot; using what is notably a <i>different</i> power to the one that lets them rip out a human's soul. If the two were one and the same then it wouldn't require different abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Elfive, I'll just grab another part of the book that's relevant. 'Lunes burn Renown into the People's souls and teach them Moon Gifts.' In case you discount lunes, this is from the introduction, 'The spiritual, supernatural part of your soul gives you a predator's instincts - and puts you on edge when you don't hunt.' Or regarding just shapeshifting, 'The body, mind, and soul shatters and reforms at once.' And gifts, 'Despite their source, Gifts are not alien powers grafted onto the soul of a werewolf.'<br /> <br /> Dave didn't say they didn't have a human soul, he said they didn't have souls. I don't believe any of us thought werewolves had human souls but I, at least, thought they had souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-28-2016, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:07:54-07:00","id":994821,"title":"","content":"Just because they <i>call</i> it a soul doesn't mean it's actually a &quot;soul&quot; in the context we're talking here. <br /> <br /> By all accounts, vampires have souls. It's what gets eaten during Diablerie. But that doesn't mean it resembles the human soul it once was any more than the vampire resembles the human they once were. <br /> <br /> Spirits and Strix basically <i>are</i> their souls. It's all mashed together in one amorphous blob with their body and mind. Werewolves are probably similar. That's probably why Empty Wolves can still use gifts. The Idigam can't get the whole thing out, because it's weird and intertwined with their flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:44:57-07:00","id":994855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994774#post994774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves don't have souls. They're part spirit. They've never been depicted having an Oneiros, but do have a connection to the deepest Astral layer somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>They occasionally have holy dreams <i>which exposes them to the Anima Mundi, </i>I'm now sure why you extrapolate from that a lack of involvement anywhere else. They are psychologically different from spirits in such a way that they very clearly have a Mind. Before their first change they are for all intents and purposes, human. With an Oneiros, and do contribute to the Temenos. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changelings have damaged souls from the thorns, when the state of them is mentioned at all. They do not have an Oneiros and are literally incapable of entering the Temenos, as per Dancers in the Dusk. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mages in the Skein</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings have great difficulty with the higher Astral Realms mages speak of. They mostly travel through a place mages call the Oneiros, but don\u2019t see it as one layer, but a huge web of Wyrd-linked dreams. Some dream threads are technically part of other \u201clayers,\u201d but changelings can\u2019t tell the difference. If an accident sends them outside the Skein of connected dreams they need help to find their way back. Sometimes they can wake up over a matter of hours, just as if they\u2019re waking up from Skeinwalking, but sometimes they sleep until they\u2019re guided home.</div> </div> </div> </div>No where in this book does it say explicitly that Changelings do not have an Oneiros, and they are not 'literally incapable of entering the Temenos', you could argue that they're incapable of doing it on their own, I'd accept that, plenty of humans cannot practically reach the Temenos on their own. But it seems quite clear here that a Changeling could end up in the Temenos and would then need help back, same as a Mage would need help navigating the Skein of Dreams.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your &quot;Correction&quot; about the Temenos falls flat because of the difference between being an active participant in making it (ie, being human, or a Beast) and being someone who doesn't have that inherent connection but intrudes into it with a power (like Demons can). That's what I was saying about &quot;having a Temenos&quot;; werewolves don't have human enough souls to participate in it, so barring unusual gifts would just skip right past it. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't actually fall flat though, because it was an argument attacking your chose of words, and the implication those choices carried. More importantly, every other supernatural splat is just as active in shaping the Temenos as a <i>Beast is</i>. They're often figures the Beast have to topple in the minds of humanity if they want to become Apex of a region, probably not a good idea to lump them and Mortal Humans together in light of that? If you come back with a Beast being able to enter the Temenos easily in such a way that enables them to take an active hand shaping it, then it's still not a good idea to lump them together, because Humans would be 'passive' participants in that case. Vampires, Werewolves, et al, do not need a power to intrude on the Temenos, your argument is on stilts, and saying anyone 'has a Temenos' is still blatantly wrong at worst, misleading at best. Werewolves already participate in the formation of the Temenos just virtue of existing.<br /> <br /> And I'm still not sure how it's supposed to benefit the game that werewolves have no real personal manifestation of their soul (or spirit). They have all the hallmarks of an interesting Oneiros, representing their struggle for Harmony and the more literal existence of touchstones, however cerebral. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or quite possibly have an entirely different astral realm all their own, before joining up to the humans again in the Anima Mundi. </div> </div> </div>There's nothing human about the Anima Mundi, aside from the remnants of Mages meddling with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Temenos doesn't belong to everyone. It belongs to humans. The <i>Anima Mundi</i> belongs to everyone. </div> </div> </div>The Temenos belongs to everyone that has a conscious sapient 'mind', or at least it should, if you're going to be reasonable about things instead of insisting that the very human memes and thought processes that power Changelings, Vampires, etc, don't impact the Astral Worlds in the same way a human's thoughts and memes do. To do otherwise would be to assert in some manner that creatures like Vampires and Werewolves are not creatures of and beholden to Mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Think of it as branching trees<br /> <br /> ( humans ) ( werewolves )<br /> <br /> Oneiros Oneiros Oneiros Oneiros Oneiros Oneiros Oneiros ??? ??? ???<br /> \\................. / .........\\............. /............ \\............. /........... /.......... \\ ....| ..../<br /> .\\................/........... \\ .........../.............. \\ .........../........... /............ \\... |... /<br /> ..-------------------------Temenos ------------------------------------ .......--?????-<br /> ................................\\ .................................................. ..................../<br /> .................................\\................ .................................................. .. /<br /> ....................................-----------Anima Mundi----------------------------<br /> <br /> If Werewolves have an astral within whatever it is they have instead of souls that permeate their entire spirit/flesh hybrid bodies, it might have analogous layers to Oneiros and Temenos, but a realm-of-an-individual-werewolf's spirit would not be an Oneiros, and a realm of all Werewolves would not be the Temenos. As far as we're concerned, the question-mark realms don't exist, and werewolves just go straight from their dreams to the Anima Mundi. But again, if you want to invent strange new worlds to explore, go for it. </div> </div> </div>If a Werewolf has a reflection of their emotions, conscious thoughts, desires, and all the other very human things they deal with every day, and it possessed a Daimon, and lesser actors to represent the clash between their Touchstones and Harmony, it would be identical to an Oneiros, and a rose by any other name would smell just as sweet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:46:52-07:00","id":994856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994776#post994776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are good game-design reasons for keeping the Oneiros and Temenos humans (and Beasts) only, foremost among them the lack of need to explain the Astral in every single game. It's there when games like Beast and Demon want to use it. It's ignorable when games like Changeling and Werewolf don't want to use it, and that's all the justification I need.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or you could just not explain it and let individual troupes decide how it functions with those groups instead of forcing them to swim up river against the flow of 'canon'?<br /> <br /> Sure, it is justification, but 'It saves us the trouble of explaining it differently for everyone' is an argument of laziness, not compelling narrative, and makes for a disjointed incoherent cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:58:11-07:00","id":994872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994821#post994821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because they <i>call</i> it a soul doesn't mean it's actually a &quot;soul&quot; in the context we're talking here.<br /> <br /> By all accounts, vampires have souls. It's what gets eaten during Diablerie. But that doesn't mean it resembles the human soul it once was any more than the vampire resembles the human they once were.<br /> <br /> Spirits and Strix basically <i>are</i> their souls. It's all mashed together in one amorphous blob with their body and mind. Werewolves are probably similar. That's probably why Empty Wolves can still use gifts. The Idigam can't get the whole thing out, because it's weird and intertwined with their flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are we ready to invent the No True Soul fallacy yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:01:42-07:00","id":994877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994821#post994821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because they <i>call</i> it a soul doesn't mean it's actually a &quot;soul&quot; in the context we're talking here.<br /> <br /> By all accounts, vampires have souls. It's what gets eaten during Diablerie. But that doesn't mean it resembles the human soul it once was any more than the vampire resembles the human they once were.<br /> <br /> Spirits and Strix basically <i>are</i> their souls. It's all mashed together in one amorphous blob with their body and mind. Werewolves are probably similar. That's probably why Empty Wolves can still use gifts. The Idigam can't get the whole thing out, because it's weird and intertwined with their flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they do have souls, then? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What <i>is</i> a soul and how do we then determine what does and does not have them?<br /> <br /> Apparently there are different <i>kinds</i> of souls that somehow do exactly the same thing as a regular soul in most respects except for the very unclear respects we are not privy to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 10-28-2016, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:02:19-07:00","id":994878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994821#post994821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because they <i>call</i> it a soul doesn't mean it's actually a &quot;soul&quot; in the context we're talking here.<br /> <br /> By all accounts, vampires have souls. It's what gets eaten during Diablerie. But that doesn't mean it resembles the human soul it once was any more than the vampire resembles the human they once were.<br /> <br /> Spirits and Strix basically <i>are</i> their souls. It's all mashed together in one amorphous blob with their body and mind. Werewolves are probably similar. That's probably why Empty Wolves can still use gifts. The Idigam can't get the whole thing out, because it's weird and intertwined with their flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And to more seriously answer your argument, Dave's assertion wasn't just that they don't have souls, it was that they are 'spirits', which as nofather pointed out repeatedly, is demonstrably untrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:03:41-07:00","id":994879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994856#post994856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sure, it is justification, but 'It saves us the trouble of explaining it differently for everyone' is an argument of laziness, not compelling narrative, and makes for a disjointed incoherent cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please do not start mixing up you criticisms. You have successfully argued that the way the Astral is structured does not fit your personal preferences, you haven't shown that there is anything incoherent about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:07:29-07:00","id":994884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994879#post994879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please do not start mixing up you criticisms. You have successfully argued that the way the Astral is structured does not fit your personal preferences, you haven't shown that there is anything incoherent about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've shown more than once that his claims are inaccurate, and in the end he comes out with 'It's easier on the writers to say they don't exist, and that's all the justification I need.&quot;<br /> <br /> More importantly, criticizing that justification is entirely valid regardless of whether or not the final result is coherent, because it's a criticism of the motivation, not the writing specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:10:09-07:00","id":994885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994884#post994884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've shown more than once that his claims are inaccurate</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you have only shown that you are incapable of quoting people correctly, somehow transforming Dave's &quot;Werewolves are part spirit&quot; into &quot;Werevolves are spirit&quot; to have an easier strawman to rail against.<br /> As long as you keep misquoting people you haven shown nothing but that there is good reason to doubt that you are arguing in good faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:16:10-07:00","id":994888,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea: Werewolves can have thoughts and emotions despite lacking an oneiros the same way that <i>real people do. </i><br /> <br /> You don't need a bunch of personifications running around in your head to be a functional human being. You just need, like, a brain. And some sort of metaphysical go-juice in CoDverse. But that doesn't need to have some complex internal structure, and certainly not one a mage can necessarily interact with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:20:29-07:00","id":994889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994885#post994885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you have only shown that you are incapable of quoting people correctly, somehow transforming Dave's &quot;Werewolves are part spirit&quot; into &quot;Werevolves are spirit&quot; to have an easier strawman to rail against.<br /> As long as you keep misquoting people you haven shown nothing but that there is good reason to doubt that you are arguing in good faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how I'm 'misquoting' him when I am copying word for word so anyone can see it. You're ignoring his erroneous comments about Changelings, Beasts, the Temenos, and how it doesn't logically follow for sapient beings to not be included in the astral realms which reflect sapient thought.<br /> <br /> He says that Werewolves have no souls and are part spirit, he's asserting that instead of having a soul they have spirits, the rest of them is 'flesh' and therefor just a body that will eventually die. It's not 'misquoting' someone to make a criticism from what logically follows what they said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:21:41-07:00","id":994890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994888#post994888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an idea: Werewolves can have thoughts and emotions despite lacking an oneiros the same way that <i>real people do. </i><br /> <br /> You don't need a bunch of personifications running around in your head to be a functional human being. You just need, like, a brain. And some sort of metaphysical go-juice in CoDverse. But that doesn't need to have some complex internal structure, and certainly not one a mage can necessarily interact with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except... that's not how it works for normal functional human beings at all. It's fundamentally untrue to the setting. Losing your soul turns you into a listless zombie. Not <i>immediately,</i> but then a mage deprived of a soul doesn't <i>immediately</i> lose contact with it for spellcasting purposes either.<br /> <br /> This is what happens to a &quot;functional&quot; human being deprived of a soul in CoD:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> THRALL (PERSISTENT)<br /> The character has fully succumbed to the effects of soullessness. She may not spend Willpower points for any reason, may not use her Defense in combat, may not spend Experiences, and suffers all the effects of the Broken Condition (see p. 314) as well. Mages can no longer cast spells. The player should only continue playing a character with this Condition if she stands a chance of regaining a soul. Resolution: Regain a soul.<br /> Beat: Gain a Beat whenever the character is victimized as a result of her Condition. </div> </div> </div>ALSO, Sleepers absolutely have Oneiroi. So yes, normal, functional human beings need them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A sorcerer in his own Oneiros is formidable; his spells never risk Paradox as long as the magic doesn\u2019t leave the confines of his own soul. This doesn\u2019t apply to shared or foreign Oneiroi. Sleepers\u2019 Oneiroi reflect their curse to a greater extent than the material realm. All magic cast in a Sleeper\u2019s Oneiros is a Paradox risk. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 10-28-2016, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:22:21-07:00","id":994891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994888#post994888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an idea: Werewolves can have thoughts and emotions despite lacking an oneiros the same way that <i>real people do. </i><br /> <br /> You don't need a bunch of personifications running around in your head to be a functional human being. You just need, like, a brain. And some sort of metaphysical go-juice in CoDverse. But that doesn't need to have some complex internal structure, and certainly not one a mage can necessarily interact with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not arguing that the Oneiros is necessary for someone to function. I'm arguing that there is no coherent reason for a werewolf to not have an Oneiros aside from Dave's justification that it's easier from a writing standpoint - which is apparently all the justification he needs. Werewolves have souls, so do vampires, and they have sapient thoughts that can be disseminated to other individuals, mortal or otherwise, that impact the astral realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":".  Edited my post because Jachra apparently 'is' arguing that X: 10-28-2016, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:24:44-07:00","id":994892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994889#post994889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how I'm 'misquoting' him when I am copying word for word so anyone can see it. You're ignoring his erroneous comments about Changelings, Beasts, the Temenos, and how it doesn't logically follow for sapient beings to not be included in the astral realms which reflect sapient thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Temenos is the astral realm of the collective soul of Humanity, not the astral realm of the collective soul of every sapient being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:33:50-07:00","id":994895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994889#post994889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see how I'm 'misquoting' him when I am copying word for word so anyone can see it. You're ignoring his erroneous comments about Changelings, Beasts, the Temenos, and how it doesn't logically follow for sapient beings to not be included in the astral realms which reflect sapient thought.<br /> <br /> He says that Werewolves have no souls and are part spirit, he's asserting that instead of having a soul they have spirits, the rest of them is 'flesh' and therefor just a body that will eventually die. It's not 'misquoting' someone to make a criticism from what logically follows what they said.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't see an erroneous statement about changelings. I can see you getting confused and thinking changeling dream combat takes place in the Oneiros, when it doesn't, and mistaking an idle theory of mine about the Hedge being the Astral Barrier as someone also meaning the Hedge is the Oneiros, when the barrier and Oneiros are, again, different things.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oneiromancy&quot; has the same root greek as &quot;Oneiros&quot;, but the one does not take place within the other.<br /> <br /> See Dream Guardians in Dancers in the Dusk, who are Oneiros creatures accidentally summoned forth into the dreamscape changelings can access. Or the Kindly stranger in the same book, which is a Temenos creature.<br /> <br /> To add to the confusion, some games refer to ghosts as &quot;restless souls&quot;, &quot;spirits of the dead&quot; and other poetic terms, when in <i>game mechanic</i> terms ghosts are not spirits, and do not have souls. Words can mean different things in different gamelines. Regardless, one <i>more</i> time, I heartily endorse you opening the astral up to other supernatural beings if that's what floats your boat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:34:42-07:00","id":994897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994891#post994891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolves have souls, so do vampires, and they have sapient thoughts that can be disseminated to other individuals, mortal or otherwise, that impact the astral realms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But they <i>dont</i> impact the astral. That's the whole point.<br /> <br /> In fact, if you look in Beast the things that can create Chambers via breaking points are listed, and the justification is that when this happens their souls draw close to the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> Prometheans losing pilgrimage counts, and prometheans explicitly <i>don't have souls. </i>That's a core premise of the game. Harmony loss doesn't.<br /> <br /> Werewolf souls have less of a connection to the astral <i>than the not-soul of a promethean</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:35:28-07:00","id":994899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994892#post994892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Temenos is the astral realm of the collective soul of Humanity, not the astral realm of the collective soul of every sapient being.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Temenos is inspired by Carl Jung's <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">collective unconscious, which was distinct from the personal unconscious, which is arguably the inspiration for the Oneiros. Nowhere in the books does it say that the Temenos is built exclusively by humans. The closest it gets is saying that most influence is from sleepers - well yes, because Sleepers drastically out number every other group. If you're going to be true to the inspiration then any sapient being with a soul who possesses a complex psychology contributes to the Temenos.<br /> <br /> Or you could just assert that it's just humans without backing it up - or even defining what is human and what isn't.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:39:10-07:00","id":994901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994899#post994899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nowhere in the books does it say that the Temenos is built exclusively by humans. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Yes it does. Literally everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:43:01-07:00","id":994904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage the Awakening Second Edition Pg. 247-248</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Temenos, <u>Soul of Humanity</u>:</b> Mages think of the Temenos as the next layer up from the Oneiros. This is where individual souls coalesce into <u>the massed soul of Humanity</u>, private thoughts becoming shared myths, archetypes, and concepts. [...]<br /> <br /> Mages travel the Temenos in search of occult insights and a better understanding of <u>human nature</u>.[...]<br /> <br /> As a mage rises through the Temenos, cultural skin flakes off collective ideas until she reaches the border of the Anima Mundi, the Omphalos or Boundary Stone: the liminal realm of High Speech that represents the highest form of human language. From here, mages can either travel through tunnels in the stone into the Anima Mundi, or skirt its edge to walk into the Primordial realms containing <u>humanity\u2019s essential emotions and fears</u>. These realms, representing the <u>animal instincts of the human race</u>, are poorly understood. Their inhabitants are typically monstrous and highly protective of their territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Underlined for my emphasis, Solana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:50:41-07:00","id":994910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994895#post994895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't see an erroneous statement about changelings. I can see you getting confused and thinking changeling dream combat takes place in the Oneiros, when it doesn't, and mistaking an idle theory of mine about the Hedge being the Astral Barrier as someone also meaning the Hedge is the Oneiros, when the barrier and Oneiros are, again, different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, goodie, let's go back to that thing I already apologized for instead of facing my actual criticisms, Dave! Brilliant! Cool!<br /> <br /> I can also be passive aggressive!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Oneiromancy&quot; has the same root greek as &quot;Oneiros&quot;, but the one does not take place within the other. </div> </div> </div>And I already conceded the point and apologized for confusing it, what's that gotta do with my argument right now?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See Dream Guardians in Dancers in the Dusk, who are Oneiros creatures accidentally summoned forth into the dreamscape changelings can access. Or the Kindly stranger in the same book, which is a Temenos creature. </div> </div> </div>You mean the Dream Guardian that is explicitly:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dancers in the Dusk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have Mage: The Awakening available, the Dream Guardian should be recognizable as being the host\u2019s daimon, the personification of their drive to self-improvement. Somehow, the Glamour expenditure has merged the dreamscape with the Oneiros, the realm of the dreamer\u2019s Soul, and the daimon has been caught up in the inrush of energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>In other words, you're saying dreams and the Oneiros never overlap, and then bringing up a specific phenomena that happens <b>when they overlap</b>. Dave. Dave seriously?<br /> <br /> The Kindly Stranger example is <i>much closer</i>: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dancers in the Dusk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Others claim to have seen the Kindly Stranger leave when fought off successfully, opening the doors of its theatre-self and striding out. These few individuals claim to have felt, rather than seen, the landscape \u201coutside\u201d; a clamor of voices that made them feel as though they were human again, if only briefly. As the dreamscape ended in absence of the Incubus, they became powerfully aware of how cut off they were from their former lives. Old writings speak of a \u201cTerminus,\u201d a place where all of humanity\u2019s stories dwell and all human interaction takes place. Perhaps the Stranger is a being from this place, a sentient play that reaches out and connects strangers in the pursuit of art without realizing it kills those it touches.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty good evidence that Changelings are cut off from the Temenos, and it's presented in a compelling fashion. It doesn't assert in any fashion that they don't have an Oneiros, however. The lack of a connection with the Temenos serves as a potential story seed, something to work toward, instead of just asserting that they're not human, so nope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To add to the confusion, some games refer to ghosts as &quot;restless souls&quot;, &quot;spirits of the dead&quot; and other poetic terms, when in <i>game mechanic</i> terms ghosts are not spirits, and do not have souls. Words can mean different things in different gamelines. Regardless, one <i>more</i> time, I heartily endorse you opening the astral up to other supernatural beings if that's what floats your boat. </div> </div> </div>That's very kind of you to give me permission, again in the most condescending fashion available to you.<br /> <br /> So you've now asserted that Werewolves don't have souls, even though the books have specified they do, without it being in the same flavor context of a 'restless soul/spirit' with ghosts. One is borrowing from common sobriquets for ghosts themselves, the other is very definitely making werewolves distinct from 'actual spirits'. You've asserted that Dancers in the Dusk says that Changelings cannot reach the Temenos (it doesn't say that, it says their connection is damaged and they have difficulty with the higher realms, this isn't a 'no' it's a 'here's a pain point, explore it.) You flat out stated that Dancers in the Dusk claims Changelings do not have an Oneiros, it never says that, anywhere. You presented Dream Guardians as though they furthered your argument that dreams and oneiroi are not connected, when the opposite is true. <br /> <br /> Are you finding it a little easier to spot the erroneous statements now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:50:48-07:00","id":994911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994899#post994899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could just assert that it's just humans without backing it up - or even defining what is human and what isn't.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>I think &quot;everyone with Integrity or Wisdom in, those with Satiety a deep and special relationship to one far-flung corner of it, everyone else is a visitor&quot; is a reasonable definition of &quot;human&quot; for purposes of what is sufficiently human to contribute to creating the Temenos.<br /> <br /> Again, though, you can visit if you're a person using Cover and have the right Exploit, or if someone with Satiety opens a Primordial Pathway around you no matter what integrity trait you use.<br /> <br /> There are many possible definitions of &quot;human&quot;. What matters for the Temenos is whether you have a human soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:51:12-07:00","id":994912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994901#post994901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Yes it does. Literally everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Citation, please?<br /> <br /> And again, please define 'Human' for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:52:30-07:00","id":994914,"title":"","content":"If you're genuinely keen for written material on werewolf souls, their dreams and how their unconscious operates, please make it clear to the people who run Onyx Path that this is a thing you'd be happy to pay for :P I'm sure there's enough of us writers who would be more than eager to wax lyrical on werewolf spirituality if we were contracted to do so!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:55:54-07:00","id":994918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994904#post994904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Underlined for my emphasis, Solana.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd argue that any sapient being who has a soul, is sapient, and so on, is effectively human. <br /> <br /> These aren't abyssal entities, they're not aliens from beyond the stars. Every one of these supernatural beings start off Human. The human element is what makes them compelling and interesting, and ultimately relatable. Certainly they're far more relatable than an actual wolf would be, or an actual leech. <br /> <br /> And I'd point out again, that the justification for deciding that they shouldn't is that it's easier on the writers. If you think that's a compelling rational, by all means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:00:25-07:00","id":994919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994914#post994914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're genuinely keen for written material on werewolf souls, their dreams and how their unconscious operates, please make it clear to the people who run Onyx Path that this is a thing you'd be happy to pay for :P I'm sure there's enough of us writers who would be more than eager to wax lyrical on werewolf spirituality if we were contracted to do so!</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope that's essentially what I'm doing in this thread. With the intensity and dedication of my arguments I've shown exactly how much I care about the inclusion of other splats in the Astral Realms, it is one of my favorite things about the game's cosmology, and cutting off a huge swath of game lines from it, when silence would be preferable, is to me a travesty. I hope as well that I've shown why it wouldn't be a stretch of the imagination to include those groups in something that important to the world's cosmology. At the least, I hope I've shown that you can do so without stretching suspension of disbelief to the breaking point.<br /> <br /> If I'm coming across as an asshole, it's because Dave seems hellbent on poking me even after I apologized to him and thanked everyone for presenting their ideas well. That sits quite poorly with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:02:57-07:00","id":994920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994918#post994918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd argue that any sapient being who has a soul, is sapient, and so on, is effectively human.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books beg to differ.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf the Forsaken Second Edition, chapter 2, the very first line</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves aren\u2019t human.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:05:24-07:00","id":994921,"title":"","content":"Okay. So you're now trying to argue with me based on sections of a changeling book <i>that I wrote</i>. I meant that the Daimon got summoned through a momentary astral prolapse, not that the dreamscape and Oneiros became the same thing for a scene, but Death of the Author and all that.<br /> <br /> And damn, Ethan cut the line about changelings bouncing off the Kindly Stranger's exit portal. Never noticed that before. Eh, doesn't matter. Changelings still can't go to the Temenos.<br /> <br /> My intent is not to be condescending. Certain cosmological concepts have gotten a bit firmer over the last ten years. Dancers even outright says in one place that Skein tunnels move through the Oneiros, which would support you. If the Skein existed any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:07:21-07:00","id":994922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994919#post994919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope that's essentially what I'm doing in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe forums are great for communicating with various people involved in the creation of various books, but if you definitely want to signal your interest to the relevant parties, you probably want to look at other avenues as well. I would guess at emailing in or the like - Dave might have a better idea than I - but the people who decide what goes on the Forsaken product schedule are presumably Stew the developer and the people above him in the chain. You probably don't want to rely on the chance that one of them happens to read this one particular thread if you want to indicate such.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:13:45-07:00","id":994925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994921#post994921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. So you're now trying to argue with me based on sections of a changeling book <i>that I wrote</i>. I meant that the Daimon got summoned through a momentary astral prolapse, not that the dreamscape and Oneiros became the same thing for a scene, but Death of the Author and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right? How dare I confront a writer with his own words, the audacity! The actual section describes the Dream Guardian forming when the Daimon - which lives in the Oneiros - doesn't appreciate the changes that the oneiropomp is making to the person's dreams. I just thought it was funny you'd use the Dream Guardian as an example when it is specifically an example of the sorts of influences dreams and the Oneiros have on each other. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994921#post994921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And damn, Ethan cut the line about changelings bouncing off the Kindly Stranger's exit portal. Never noticed that before. Eh, doesn't matter. Changelings still can't go to the Temenos.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Man, that thing I wrote didn't make it into the final cut, eh, whatever, I'm still right because I said so.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sound argumentative skills there, Dave.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My intent is not to be condescending. Certain cosmological concepts have gotten a bit firmer over the last ten years. Dancers even outright says in one place that Skein tunnels move through the Oneiros, which would support you. If the Skein existed any more. </div> </div> </div>And until something contradicts its existence, I don't see why that wouldn't still be the case. A new edition doesn't completely retcon every setting element from the previous books, otherwise there's a lot of Vampire, Mage, and Changeling books that people just shouldn't buy anymore, at least not unless they're going to use them exclusively with the 1st edition.<br /> <br /> Somehow I doubt Onyx Path would support that strategy. <br /> <br /> And whether you meant to be or not, you were, extremely so. When I offended you, I apologized, when you offended me, you go: &quot;Eh, whatever. If it works for you that's cool, Bro.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:16:06-07:00","id":994927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994922#post994922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThe forums are great for communicating with various people involved in the creation of various books, but if you definitely want to signal your interest to the relevant parties, you probably want to look at other avenues as well. I would guess at emailing in or the like - Dave might have a better idea than I - but the people who decide what goes on the Forsaken product schedule are presumably Stew the developer and the people above him in the chain. You probably don't want to rely on the chance that one of them happens to read this one particular thread if you want to indicate such.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there are specific emails in question for recommending books we'd like to see, I would love to have it. I work a lot of customer service/moderation that include message boards, so I'm just accustomed to my bosses seeing it, especially when it's a larger thread like this one.<br /> <br /> I apologize for my presumptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:17:47-07:00","id":994929,"title":"","content":"Actually, that is something I want to bring up. You seem to be reading me as pissing on the concept of astral werewolves and condescending to say &quot;change it in your own game.&quot; Which pains me, as I personally agree with you. The more Astral the merrier! The reason Beast uses the Astral Realms is partly because I enthused about it to Matt and helped with the tricksier cosmic bits, because I always thought it was a shame only Mage used it and wanted it to become a shared setting space like the Hisil and Underworld.<br /> <br /> Changeling doesn't use the Astral Realms because it has its own cosmology going on with the Hedge. The other games just don't have the crossover room necessary to look at it and describe how their protagonists perceive the inner worlds. We put things like &quot;werewolves totally dream themselves into the Anima Mundi and never even notice&quot; and &quot;Changing Breeds have no separation between the Temenos and Anima Mundi&quot; into books as throwaway references because it's <i>cool</i>.<br /> <br /> But I can't hold Stew down and force him to use it (he's bigger than me) any more than I can get David to chuck the Hedge out and spend the wordcount on having changelings use the same mental spaces as mages and beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:26:09-07:00","id":994933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And until something contradicts its existence, I don't see why that wouldn't still be the case. A new edition doesn't completely retcon every setting element from the previous books, otherwise there's a lot of Vampire, Mage, and Changeling books that people just shouldn't buy anymore, at least not unless they're going to use them exclusively with the 1st edition. </div> </div> </div>Er... Yes. Sorry. There are lots of things in 1st ed books for all three of those games that either aren't &quot;true&quot; any more or require work. Even aside from things like Requiem currently having three different sets of rules for the Strix, two sorts of Gargoyles, etc. The extra coil levels in Ordo Dracul no longer work with the Coils given in Requiem second edition. Magical Traditions is now only good as a source of yantra inspiration. Lots of early mage books assume Atlantis had a historical existence, when it didn't. Such are the realities of rpg editions, much as we try to keep <i>most</i> things useful.<br /> <br /> This may be a spoiler, but the way changelings interact with dreams is changing in second edition so that it revolves around the Hedge rather than being off on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:27:32-07:00","id":994934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994929#post994929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, that is something I want to bring up. You seem to be reading me as pissing on the concept of astral werewolves and condescending to say &quot;change it in your own game.&quot; Which pains me, as I personally agree with you. The more Astral the merrier! The reason Beast uses the Astral Realms is partly because I enthused about it to Matt and helped with the tricksier cosmic bits, because I always thought it was a shame only Mage used it and wanted it to become a shared setting space like the Hisil and Underworld.<br /> <br /> Changeling doesn't use the Astral Realms because it has its own cosmology going on with the Hedge. The other games just don't have the crossover room necessary to look at it and describe how their protagonists perceive the inner worlds. We put things like &quot;werewolves totally dream themselves into the Anima Mundi and never even notice&quot; and &quot;Changing Breeds have no separation between the Temenos and Anima Mundi&quot; into books as throwaway references because it's <i>cool</i>.<br /> <br /> But I can't hold Stew down and force him to use it (he's bigger than me) any more than I can get David to chuck the Hedge out and spend the wordcount on having changelings use the same mental spaces as mages and beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Goodness I wish that were the case. I can't tell you how many times I read your Awakened Inspirations post, which included Promethea, which led me to <i>read</i> it.<br /> <br /> It will always be the case for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:38:07-07:00","id":994939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994920#post994920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books beg to differ.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the distinction rings arbitrary, because werewolves are typically most comfortable in their human forms, grow up as humans, have human passions, aspirations, hopes, and care about their human families (albeit with a dynamic different from most humans - and yet I know plenty of humans who empathize with the pack and family dynamics in werewolf). They are written by and for humans to explore behavior deemed inhuman, I'd argue it's there whether we want it to be or not.<br /> <br /> One of the most compelling things about the Chronicles of Darkness is that it is a setting of human monsters, and every one of the splats has something meaningful to say and communicate about being human. Using the excuse that they're not human in order to justify denying the existence of an entire area of cosmology shoots the game in both feet, instead of just one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994929#post994929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, that is something I want to bring up. You seem to be reading me as pissing on the concept of astral werewolves and condescending to say &quot;change it in your own game.&quot; Which pains me, as I personally agree with you. The more Astral the merrier! The reason Beast uses the Astral Realms is partly because I enthused about it to Matt and helped with the tricksier cosmic bits, because I always thought it was a shame only Mage used it and wanted it to become a shared setting space like the Hisil and Underworld.<br /> <br /> Changeling doesn't use the Astral Realms because it has its own cosmology going on with the Hedge. The other games just don't have the crossover room necessary to look at it and describe how their protagonists perceive the inner worlds. We put things like &quot;werewolves totally dream themselves into the Anima Mundi and never even notice&quot; and &quot;Changing Breeds have no separation between the Temenos and Anima Mundi&quot; into books as throwaway references because it's <i>cool</i>.<br /> <br /> But I can't hold Stew down and force him to use it (he's bigger than me) any more than I can get David to chuck the Hedge out and spend the wordcount on having changelings use the same mental spaces as mages and beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like that aspect of Beast and I'm glad you sparked that. I apologize for calling you, effectively, a lazy writer. I do still feel that not wanting to explore the territory from a development standpoint is justification for simply leaving it unexplored, rather than stating firmly that it's 'not there to be explored'.<br /> <br /> I'd also argue that the Hedge and the Astral Realms are as capable of existing together as Pandemonium and Arcadia are, but that's an entirely different matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994933#post994933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Er... Yes. Sorry. There are lots of things in 1st ed books for all three of those games that either aren't &quot;true&quot; any more or require work. Even aside from things like Requiem currently having three different sets of rules for the Strix, two sorts of Gargoyles, etc. The extra coil levels in Ordo Dracul no longer work with the Coils given in Requiem second edition. Magical Traditions is now only good as a source of yantra inspiration. Lots of early mage books assume Atlantis had a historical existence, when it didn't. Such are the realities of rpg editions, much as we try to keep <i>most</i> things useful.<br /> <br /> This may be a spoiler, but the way changelings interact with dreams is changing in second edition so that it revolves around the Hedge rather than being off on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but every one of those is an example of 'true until contradicted', there's still a lot of material to make use of in second edition that exists in those books - until something in second edition contradicts it. It can be a bit limiting if we're expected to ignore the existing body of work when Vampire 2nd edition doesn't have a fully published supplement in the time since it has come out. If that helps explain my position a bit clearer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":".  Edited for some really bad grammar in the first paragraph. 10-28-2016, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:55:28-07:00","id":994949,"title":"","content":"Perhaps much like they lack a distinction between soul and body, the internal shared soul of the spirits is also external to them.<br /> <br /> So basically the werewolf version of the Temenos is the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:56:53-07:00","id":994951,"title":"","content":"Or the Gauntlet!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:59:37-07:00","id":994954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994951#post994951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the Gauntlet!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The hooks dropped in the Dark Eras supplement regarding Luna and the Gauntlet are some of my favorite parts from that period. :c","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T17:48:13-07:00","id":994975,"title":"","content":"I know this is about Werewolves primarily, but I can't help looking at the talk of non-humans lacking an Oneiros/Temenos but think of some of the (admittedly 1e) references of Vampires ending up in the Underworld when in Torpor, and so for 2e thinking that Kindred dreams first take place in or 'near' the Grave Dream realm there, despite being 'new', and so border the Underworld like typical dreams border the Oneiros (and yet still also border the Hedge, because the Hedge and Underworld connect at points anyway). So, if you tried forcing your way into a Vampire's 'Oneiros' you really just push yourself right into the Lower Depths.<br /> <br /> The ideas and mechanics there would need some work, but it could be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T17:55:44-07:00","id":994981,"title":"","content":"Werewolf 2e makes quite a few explicit references to the Forsaken as having souls, so I&quot;m not sure what all the debate is here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:30:17-07:00","id":995015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994951#post994951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the Gauntlet!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, though, are we going to get any more material on the Gauntlet-dwelling critters? Aside from a brief mention in Summoners, they don't seem to have been developed a lot, and it was a cool idea that I'd love to see more of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T21:30:44-07:00","id":995069,"title":"","content":"I believe azlu 'hives' are meant to extend somewhat into the Gauntlet. Could just be head canon but I believe it was mentioned somewhere.<br /> <br /> So, little intelligent spiders that just want to crawl in your nose, eat your brain, and ride your body around like a mecha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T23:28:33-07:00","id":995096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994951#post994951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the Gauntlet!</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the implementation that the collective souls of werewolves form the Gauntlet and keep the worlds of Flesh and Spirit apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T00:52:13-07:00","id":995106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994951#post994951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the Gauntlet!</div> </div> </div> </div>This would imply that previous Temenos equivalent for Uratha was Pangea - and with her lost in prehistory, I'm not sure it rubs me right way...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T01:17:24-07:00","id":995116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994981#post994981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf 2e makes quite a few explicit references to the Forsaken as having souls, so I&quot;m not sure what all the debate is here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the debate is whether Werewolf use the word &quot;soul&quot; the same way Mage uses the word &quot;soul.&quot; See also: occasional descriptions of ghosts having/being souls and Mummy's five distinct souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T01:27:56-07:00","id":995121,"title":"","content":"<b>Next argument why Gauntlet = Werewolf Temenos is bad idea</b> - At least 1/3rd of race is actively working against Gauntlet. Yes, I mean here Pure Tribes. Thinking their collective souls would sustain this Flesh and Spirits barrier is wrong...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T02:32:08-07:00","id":995127,"title":"","content":"Also, in <b>CoD</b> universe, you have multiple 'souls-types' - human ( and mages ) souls are one. Vampires are other, after Embrace. Werewolves are others. Changelings souls <i>were </i>humans once, but now they are filled with Glamour. Sin Eaters had human souls once, but now they are in symbiozis with Giests. Etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T03:26:57-07:00","id":995139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=995121#post995121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Next argument why Gauntlet = Werewolf Temenos is bad idea</b> - At least 1/3rd of race is actively working against Gauntlet. Yes, I mean here Pure Tribes. Thinking their collective souls would sustain this Flesh and Spirits barrier is wrong...</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't make it wrong. It just makes that 1/3 misguided, which they already are, the Gauntlet is a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T03:51:52-07:00","id":995143,"title":"","content":"I think the idea is more that the gauntlet/Pangaea is the werewolf (or rather, Pangaean, but werewolves are the only ones left) temenos irrespective of it's current form. <br /> <br /> Perhaps it would be more accurate to say it's <i>both</i>. The werewolf branch of the astral tree has four sections, not three. You got their oneroi, which are also kind of their bodies; the gauntlet, which is what's left of the pangaean temenos and probably the reason for their current anger issues because a chunk of their soul has basically collapsed. Then the shadow is the temenos of them <i>and</i> spirits, a sort of soul of most of the world except humans. Then logically it would be possible to meditate into the Anima Mundi from certain parts of the shadow. Probably a really deep Place-That-Isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T05:49:17-07:00","id":995166,"title":"","content":"My personal headcanon is that Vampires and Werewolves absolutely have an Oneiros. It may not be a 'Human' Oneiros for the sake of effects that are designed to target 'Human' Oneiros, but they are places that can be visited with the appropriate supernatural effects and have suitably thematic atmospheres.<br /> <br /> Why? Because the potential for story hooks is <u><i><b>ABSOLUTELY MASSIVE</b></i></u>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T07:24:17-07:00","id":995185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=995139#post995139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't make it wrong. It just makes that 1/3 misguided, which they already are, the Gauntlet is a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, good for humans. Werewolves, spirits and Pangaeans seemed to have a lot more fun back before the Sundering, plus, Pangaeans kind of lost their cool Arcana and partially Fleshy status and got stuck with being boring ol' spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T07:55:56-07:00","id":995194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=995185#post995185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, good for humans. Werewolves, spirits and Pangaeans seemed to have a lot more fun back before the Sundering, plus, Pangaeans kind of lost their cool Arcana and partially Fleshy status and got stuck with being boring ol' spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a nutshell - Creation of Gauntlet should be massive 'wound' to spirits half of werewolves souls....<br /> <br /> I still thinks that Shadow works better as 'Temeons for Uratha'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-29-2016, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T08:03:23-07:00","id":995200,"title":"","content":"Or weird flesh things like the Hosts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T10:23:09-07:00","id":995249,"title":"","content":"And if we're going with Gauntlet and Shadow standing in for Werewolf Temenos, then can we make the Underworld the ghost, Sin-Eater, and possibly Vampire Temenos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T10:30:48-07:00","id":995253,"title":"","content":"Makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T10:47:57-07:00","id":995704,"title":"","content":"I would like to see ideas around a Vampire's Oneiros being a realm where his &quot;Man&quot; is being hunted by his &quot;Beast&quot;. Or maybe his Oneiros was invaded by the Beast (not the Primordial) after the Embrace, and it activaly destroyed his connections to Temenos and is trying to hunt down and kill the &quot;Man&quot; (maybe his Daimon?).<br /> <br /> As for Werewolves, I'm perfectly fine with the idea that the Gauntlet (which once was Pangaea) is their Oneiros. It connects with the Hisil, which would be then their Temenos, and we have some references for beings being able to go from the Hisil to the Anima Mundi. Maybe then, Father Wolf was an amalgamation of Uratha instincts that grew weaker as their connections to humanity grew stronger, since instincts gave way to rational thought, killing the mighty Wolf-God and with him the forces that kept Pagaea (Uratha Oneiros) together. This would imply an even tighter connection to Mage, since Pangaean souls could create Demesnes, and they had access to Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T10:52:25-07:00","id":995707,"title":"","content":"How would other Pangaeans, like Fox or Mountain, fit in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T10:59:12-07:00","id":995709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=995707#post995707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would other Pangaeans, like Fox or Mountain, fit in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the link to the Anima Mundi was so strong there, that all things &quot;not human&quot; could dream-up their &quot;Gods&quot;? Like Pangaea was a realm slowly bleeding through the Omphalos Stones. Maybe anything with certain &quot;soul traits&quot;, like Harmony and some others long forgotten, could use Pangaea as their &quot;Oneiros&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: Bull's Children, and any other shape-shifters would use it as their Oneiros. Maybe every Pangaean had a shape-shifting race tyed to Humanity at that time, but as they were hunted by Mages and by the Wolf God, they all perished, extinct by the first draft of Darwinian law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5446,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","user":"BinAly","date":". 10-30-2016, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T11:03:15-07:00","id":995710,"title":"","content":"So you're shifting Pangaeans from the foundations of the world to dreams of it.<br /> <br /> But how does that add in to a Gauntlet? The only ones who care about a separation of spirit and flesh are Forsaken, and even then not all of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T11:20:40-07:00","id":995716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=995143#post995143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea is more that the gauntlet/Pangaea is the werewolf (or rather, Pangaean, but werewolves are the only ones left) temenos irrespective of it's current form.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it would be more accurate to say it's <i>both</i>. The werewolf branch of the astral tree has four sections, not three. You got their oneroi, which are also kind of their bodies; the gauntlet, which is what's left of the pangaean temenos and probably the reason for their current anger issues because a chunk of their soul has basically collapsed. Then the shadow is the temenos of them <i>and</i> spirits, a sort of soul of most of the world except humans. Then logically it would be possible to meditate into the Anima Mundi from certain parts of the shadow. Probably a really deep Place-That-Isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought &quot;you could run right into the Anima Mundi by going to the correct parts of the deep, deep Shadow&quot; was canon in 1e, although for the life of me I can't remember which book it's in. It might have sent you into a different realm, but I can't think of one that would fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T11:22:14-07:00","id":995717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=995710#post995710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're shifting Pangaeans from the foundations of the world to dreams of it.<br /> <br /> But how does that add in to a Gauntlet? The only ones who care about a separation of spirit and flesh are Forsaken, and even then not all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember reading in Dark Eras that the Gauntlet is what is leftover from Pangaea, or more exactly, it is a new state of the Border Marches, without the sheer power of Father Wolf to hold it open. This always meant, for me, that even if the Pure had success in returning Pangaea to it's full glory, it would only mean a return to the state of the world 5 thousand years ago, when the Border Marches allowed an easier crossing because they were uncompressed into the present Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> So, if Humans/Mages go like this -&gt; Oneiros -&gt; Temenos -&gt; Omphalos -&gt; Anima Mundi<br /> Werewolves would go like this -&gt; Border Marches/Gauntlet -&gt; Hisil -&gt; Omphalos -&gt; Anima Mundi<br /> <br /> I don't feel like changing them to &quot;dreams of the world&quot; feels right, though. It would seem that they dreamt the world, not the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T16:31:01-07:00","id":995859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=995716#post995716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought &quot;you could run right into the Anima Mundi by going to the correct parts of the deep, deep Shadow&quot; was canon in 1e, although for the life of me I can't remember which book it's in. It might have sent you into a different realm, but I can't think of one that would fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be the &quot;The Shadow Gate&quot; sidebar on p137 of Astral Realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T16:39:45-07:00","id":995864,"title":"","content":"Am I misremembering, or does Beast say that you can access all the other supernatural realms from the Dream? I might be extrapolating from how it's easier for Beasts to go from the dream to other realms than to earth, but it does make sense. We've got a connection between the deep shadow and the Dream, we've got an obvious one between the dream and the Hedge/Arcadia, and Book of the Dead has a Dead Domain that connects to it (the Grave Dream).<br /> <br /> The Machine's various shards and splinters are another case. I like the idea that the astral/the dream connects alternate universes and timelines, but I'm not sure if there's anything about that, it's been a while since I read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-31-2016, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T16:45:01-07:00","id":995867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=995864#post995864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I misremembering, or does Beast say that you can access all the other supernatural realms from the Dream?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Pathways are connections between worlds, threaded through the Primordial Dream and touching all of the realms within the Chronicles of Darkness.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T16:47:11-07:00","id":995868,"title":"","content":"It makes sense, as things like the Hisil and Underworld would be scary memories and nightmares for humans who had knowledge of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T08:43:43-07:00","id":996090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=995868#post995868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes sense, as things like the Hisil and Underworld would be scary memories and nightmares for humans who had knowledge of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or, we use the same logic from Beast that says that all the other supernaturals are their relatives and apply that to locations saying that all of the other realms are just hyper specialized Lairs that have become their own things. Beast Supremacy yo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T10:20:24-07:00","id":996135,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem there is that Horrors and the Primordial Dream are specifically spawned from human sources. While the Shadow and, at least in first edition, the Hedge have existed since before the rise of humans.<br /> <br /> That said, either way you still have a connection and the Beast's 'relations.' A werewolf inflicts Lunacy, which causes nightmares, and eventually leads to a Horror. The Horror 'claims' someone, and you have a Beast that is related to a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}